From 72678bfb2b4f04db23fcd84b7b2a1c5125218246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 20:53:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07307/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5730: CNN held-out AUROC
 is action-id base-rate + seed-luck mirage

Applies exp5727's action-id-only base-rate control to SmallFrameChangeCNN's own
held-out AUROC (exp4547's 0.709-vs-chance). Multi-seed (5) on the current corpus:
action_id_only_auroc 0.549 > CNN mean 0.539, frame_adds_over_action_id -0.010
(matching exp5727's linear-classifier -0.039). The apparent click_head win was
seed luck (0.918 on seed 4547; min 0.444 across seeds; untrained random-init
baseline mean 0.580 exceeds trained 0.570). No robust non-base-rate signal in
either head. Closes the exp5590->5728->5729 chain: the CNN is redundant with the
memory term, so no weight/gate change could bank a level. Adversarial-verify clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
